<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caesar Rodney</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1728–1784</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caesar Rodney was an American politician from Delaware and a signer of the Declaration of Independence. On the night of 1–2 July 1776 he rode about 80 miles to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a> to break a tie in Delaware's delegation and cast its vote for independence. He later commanded Delaware's militia and served as the state's president from 1778 to 1781.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/caesar-rodney.jpg" alt="Caesar Rodney" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: maybe John Thomas Scharf · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CaesarRodney_(cropped).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
